\pard\plain \tx562\tx1123\tx1685\tx2246\tx2808\tx3370\tx3931\tx4493\tx5054\tx5616\tx6178\tx6739\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs20\b0\i0 Vine-trellised, brown brick patio.}
\par\plain \f0\fs20\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0  as if his sincerity lived somewhere in the distance between them, and she was squeezing it out.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 If only Pel\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s damned smirk, that witchy smirk, full of feminine wiles and dark amusement, didn\u8217\'92t root him to the spot.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Because I am a witch.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri dropped the shim and the little clay jar. He laughed a nervous laugh, hoping she would laugh too, but she didn\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t. Obviously, she was a witch. No woman in this part of the world could look like }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 that}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0 . And the way she talked, with all that confidence\hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 there was a maturity in her posture which he shouldn\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t have missed.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93I can see myself liking you,\u8221\'94 Pel said. Her statement was almost lost amidst the cacophony of animal screams.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh,\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered as he matched her gaze. \u8220\'93What?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93You care for that animal\u8217\'92s suffering. I do, too.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Then why didn\u8217\'92t you buy it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Pel slid off her stool. \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Because I can see the bigger picture.\u8221\'94 She wandered over to the easel. She gave Vigram\u8217\'92s painting the chuckle it deserved, then studied the paint on the palette as if those mindless swirls were a truer work of art.}}